{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha","id":1418934,"title":"Help understanding the Raksha","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-18T21:42:48-07:00","id":1418934,"title":"Help understanding the Raksha","content":"I came in around very late 2e and am most familiar with 3e's take on the setting. Going back through 1e and looking over their depictions later on I've more or less wrapped my head around the various spirits and creatures in Exalted, where they come from, and what they do.<br /> <br /> However, the Raksha have always been weird to me, not in terms of their origin or nature which I get, but more what they can do and how they affect Creation. What is their role and why are they so feared? The 3e isn't super clear and I've found the information gleaned from reading about them just reinforces the idea that they seem to be a thing that has no place outside the wyld, their abilities seem weak in creation, am I missing something? I actually have 1e fair folk but I keep putting it down because I can't seem to figure them out, seeming more focused on being player characters who go around wyld shaping.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping I can get a few questions answered, I'm not trying to get their 3e version (which I know isn't out yet), more just trying to figure out what to do with them as NPCs:<br /> -Can they naturally change shape?<br /> <br /> -Do they die when killed or need extra work like spirits do?<br /> <br /> -Are they considered 'spirits'?<br /> <br /> -When a raksha is born do they decide their station or is it based on strength when they take form?<br /> <br /> -Do grace's exist in any physical sense like in CtL or are they just weird virtues?<br /> <br /> -Is there a consistancy to their appearance (ears, elemental or beast traits, etc.) that makes them recognizable? 1e player's guide stated this but I don't know if it stuck around, and I'm uncertain how they would be distinguished from elementals if so.<br /> <br /> -Can they shed their shape for power at the expense of their identity (question inspired by kill 6 billion demons)?<br /> <br /> -I know they are very good at shaping in the wyld but what kind of power would they have outside of it? I've seen mentions that they're rather weak but that seems odd considering the fear around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 10-19-2020, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T22:58:09-07:00","id":1418940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha#post1418934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Can they naturally change shape?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha#post1418934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Do they die when killed or need extra work like spirits do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all spirits need extra work to kill. First circle demons as well as many elementals just die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha#post1418934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Are they considered 'spirits'?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha#post1418934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-When a raksha is born do they decide their station or is it based on strength when they take form?</div> </div> </div> </div>I somehow doubt they decide their own station when they are formed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha#post1418934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Do grace's exist in any physical sense like in CtL or are they just weird virtues?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe the graces are physical things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha#post1418934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Is there a consistancy to their appearance (ears, elemental or beast traits, etc.) that makes them recognizable? 1e player's guide stated this but I don't know if it stuck around, and I'm uncertain how they would be distinguished from elementals if so.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's stuff that you can point to as being common among fey, like pointy ears are pretty typical, but nothing that you can be certain of, and it varies by region. It's likely that people in an area with a lot of contact fairies locally know the most common ways to distinguish them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha#post1418934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Can they shed their shape for power at the expense of their identity (question inspired by kill 6 billion demons)?</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually kind of can, but only in the very depths of the Wyld, and only ones that have incredible power. I'm not sure those would by classified as &quot;raksha&quot; though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha#post1418934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-I know they are very good at shaping in the wyld but what kind of power would they have outside of it? I've seen mentions that they're rather weak but that seems odd considering the fear around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of the Wyld, like in the static boundries of Creation, they have whatever power they can muster to bring with them. There was one instance called the Balorian Crusade where a mighty fey creature known as Prince Balor, who is equal in power to the Unconquered Sun or Ligier. Again, not 100% sure he was classified as &quot;raksha&quot; but there can definitely be incredibly powerful ones. Just look at the Fair Folk Cataphract from the book, and know that he's just a knight of the raksha nobles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T23:26:12-07:00","id":1418944,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> I'm still kind of confused as to how to actually use them though.<br /> <br /> I'm aware that alot of their power comes from the ability to shape things in the Wyld, but when it comes to using them as NPCs I'm kind of baffled.<br /> <br /> Like if I'm running, say, a dynasty game, and they end up in a fight with a Raksha in creation, I don't really know how to run them. I have no real clue about how to distinguish them visually, how to decide what kinds of powers would be at their disposal or even how to be certain they are dead, I think a lot of my difficulty is that unlike a lot of other creatures, the Raksha books were written to be player facing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aside from wyld shaping and feeding on virtues/intimicies what are some notable traits about them that would be seen in creation or the bordermarches?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T23:38:42-07:00","id":1418949,"title":"","content":"As much as Exalted\u2019s \u201cfair folk\u201d allegedly aren\u2019t meant to necessarily take after their mythological namesakes, they do so well more than often enough to just run with it as an ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T23:58:45-07:00","id":1418952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha?p=1418944#post1418944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks.Aside from wyld shaping and feeding on virtues/intimicies what are some notable traits about them that would be seen in creation or the bordermarches?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well they're beings born out of a sea of infinite potential and change, so trying to pin down commonalities there might be a bad road to go down. If anything the thing that joins them all together is that they're so different. As the book says about their cataphracts:<br /> <br /> &quot;Cataphracts vary in appearance, though coteries<br /> and courts tend to share similar forms. They may be leonine<br /> desert riders with eyes of fire, queenly warriors astride<br /> winged nightmare-beasts, or owl-faced knights driving<br /> chariots pulled by naked mortals&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically just make them freaking weird and you should be good. You won't find any Raksha that just look like normal people hanging out with normal animals.<br /> <br /> They're also kind of fond of stories and stuff usually. Like rather than have goals and wishes of their own necessarily they prefer to play roles in stories. That's not a 100% always thing, it's just something they do sometimes. So like a Raksha might go on a crusade into Creation not because he wants to kill people, but because he wants to play the role of a crusader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T01:38:50-07:00","id":1418964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha?p=1418940#post1418940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe the graces are physical things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, at least in previous editions, they <i>were </i>physical things, and could even be artifacts. (In fact, if a raksha had artifact dots they'd almost certainly be in the form of other raksha's Graces.)<br /> <br /> \u200bHowever, there was no point in physically <i>taking</i> another raksha's Graces in the Wyld if you were, yourself, a Fair Folk, because they could just dicelessly shape it back to themselves; you either had to take ownership of that Grace in shaping combat, get them to grant it to you, or get one of the Creation-born to take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-19-2020, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T01:54:47-07:00","id":1418967,"title":"","content":"Here's my take, which I think is mostly canon as of 3rd edition:<br /> <br /> Raksha are a type of being that emerged from the Wyld an attacked Creation at the end of the 1st age, when it was weakened by the Great Contagion. There are other types of creature in the Wyld, many of which the Raksha have enslaved as servants or warriors. <br /> <br /> The Raksha that currently live in Creation are exiles. Having failed to destroy Creation, they are now trapped here. This may be because, having taken on fixed shape in order to attack Creation, they found it impossible to go back. Or it may be because a new type of being has arisen within the Wyld which preys on them.<br /> <br /> They vary considerably from one another in terms of appearance and behaviour but there are a few consistencies: They are usually humanoid but with inhuman (animal or elemental) features, they are almost always incredibly beautiful, and they usually put on the airs of aristocracy - organizing themselves into courts and surrounding themselves with servants. Their servants and warmonsters follow a similar theme, but tend to be more phantasmagorical - beasts and elements blended together in a nightmare, religious vision, an acid trip.<br /> <br /> Raksha sustain themselves by feeding on emotions. Typically, they provoke those emotions in mortals by raiding to create terror or seduction to create love or lust, but other feelings are equally sustaining so long as they are passionate. They often kidnap mortals to more easily feed on them. Having one's emotions fed on by a Raksha repeatedly over a long period is damaging to the mind and/or soul, and eventually results in a mortal which lacks the capacity for emotion and therefore volition, known as a Dream-Eaten. This kind of thing gives Raksha a bad reputation, and most people try to avoid them, with mixed success. <br /> <br /> Raksha can demonstrate a wide variety of different powers, but they tend to be either inhuman beauty, skill, and grace (representated by massive dice pools), power over emotions (social effects, particularly to inspire emotions and create intimacies), and power to create things out of ambient emotion and wyld energy (for example, a Raksha knight might be able to create swarms of warrior-creatures born from nightmares). Other powers are very possible.<br /> <br /> They are vulnerable to iron but apparently not steel, for some reason. They extent of this vulnerability varies.<br /> <br /> Thematically, they are a blend of the most epic European fairy stories (my go to is the elves from Poul Anderson's Broken Sword), decadent exiled nobility, and the most dramatic cape-swooshy kind of vampire. <br /> <br /> The art usually depicts them as having gigantic Record of Lodoss War-style elf ears.<br /> <br /> To use them as NPCs, figure out an interesting method of provoking strong emotions (maybe this one traps mortals and makes them play games for their lives, feeding on the terror, elation and despair elicited by rolls of the dice) and then come up with a couple of strange aesthetic features. Then use the stats for the Cataphract or Lorelei from the corebook, depending on whether they are more social or more combat oriented.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3174-carl-ollivier","name":"Carl.ollivier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T08:49:59-07:00","id":1419009,"title":"","content":"Discworld is a very different setting from Creation, but its version of elves isn\u2019t too far off thematically.<br /> <br /> You can also take basically any fairy tale and amp up the predatory threat level, particularly in the North and East. The Big Bad Wolf becomes a pack of gorgeous wolf-themed warriors who become fascinated with a victim and start impersonating people in her life to gaslight and terrify her. Children find themselves drawn to a candy-castle, where all their needs are taken care of by the queen and her servants until their emotions are fully-consumed. The Pied Piper shows up at villages bedeviled by rat-hobgoblins, appearing to be a normal man, and offers help in exchange for a terrible price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 10-19-2020, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T09:58:49-07:00","id":1419029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha?p=1418944#post1418944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks.<br /> I'm still kind of confused as to how to actually use them though.<br /> <br /> I'm aware that alot of their power comes from the ability to shape things in the Wyld, but when it comes to using them as NPCs I'm kind of baffled.<br /> <br /> Like if I'm running, say, a dynasty game, and they end up in a fight with a Raksha in creation, I don't really know how to run them. I have no real clue about how to distinguish them visually, how to decide what kinds of powers would be at their disposal or even how to be certain they are dead, I think a lot of my difficulty is that unlike a lot of other creatures, the Raksha books were written to be player facing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans are scared of sharks. Very few humans are harmed by sharks each year, but sharks can harm humans. They're (or at least can be) bigger, stronger and faster than us.<br /> <br /> Fae are bigger, stronger, faster... smarter. And they actively predate humans.<br /> <br /> They are the terrifying stuff of myth and nightmare.<br /> <br /> The hag in the bog. The troll under the bridge. The knights of thunder and shadows who steal the breath of little children. The evil spirit that stalks the winter feasts. The giants who live in the wild places.<br /> <br /> The 3E corebook gives some sample creatures of the wyld, complete with powers. And HDNP gives a great raksha noble.<br /> <br /> Exalted can usually beat the snot out of them one-on-one.<br /> <br /> So, to challenge a circle, you'll need several. Or something the fae is good at that the circle is bad at.<br /> <br /> Creation is meant to be mysterious. When you run an encounter with The Knights of Leodine and describe them as men with the heads of lions, the PCs aren't supposed to know if they're fae or beastmen or gods or demons. Don't worry about making things fit in neat catagories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T10:20:47-07:00","id":1419034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha?p=1419029#post1419029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creation is meant to be mysterious. When you run an encounter with The Knights of Leodine and describe them as men with the heads of lions, the PCs aren't supposed to know if they're fae or beastmen or gods or demons. Don't worry about making things fit in neat catagories.</div> </div> </div> </div>EXCELLENT advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T13:07:59-07:00","id":1419072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carl.ollivier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418934-help-understanding-the-raksha?p=1418967#post1418967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Raksha that currently live in Creation are exiles. Having failed to destroy Creation, they are now trapped here. This may be because, having taken on fixed shape in order to attack Creation, they found it impossible to go back. Or it may be because a new type of being has arisen within the Wyld which preys on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must quibble with this - some Raksha may be trapped in creation, but 3E is clear that Raksha are not just trapped here and have positive reasons to run around causing trouble: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3E Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fair Folk love Creation, for it beguiles them and fills their essential emptiness\u2014an emptiness of which they were never aware, until Creation existed to contrast them. The raksha are soulless, donning ethics and passions like masks and fashion; they\u2019re not real the way a mortal is real, and must endlessly invent themselves. To immerse in the life of Creation\u2014and dine upon Creation-born souls\u2014provides another, intoxicating existence, which many fae throw themselves into wholeheartedly. The souls and sagas of heroes satisfy them best of all, drawing Fair Folk to the Exalted in endless cycles of savage war and equally savage love.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}